1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,868
Hi, Laura - could you spare a few minutes to talk about the work placement you did last summer?

2
00:00:04,868 --> 00:00:06,490
I'm thinking of doing one myself.

3
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:08,910
Hi, Tim. Sure.

4
00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:13,500
Didn't you do yours at an environmental services company?

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:17,580
That's right... It's only a very small company

6
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,434
and they needed someone to produce a company brochure,

7
00:00:20,434 --> 00:00:23,697
and I wanted to get some business experience

8
00:00:23,697 --> 00:00:29,000
because I'm interested in a career in occupational psychology in a business environment.

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,130
It was good because I had overall responsibility for the project.

10
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:38,160
What kind of skills do you think you developed on the placement?

11
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:41,287
I mean, apart from the ones you already had...

12
00:00:41,287 --> 00:00:46,500
Did you have to do all the artwork for the brochure, the layout and everything?

13
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,450
We hired the services of a professional photographer for that.

14
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:54,540
I did have to use my IT skills to a certain extent

15
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:58,220
because I cut and pasted text from marketing leaflets,

16
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:01,550
but that didn't involve anything I hadn't done before.

17
00:01:01,550 --> 00:01:06,620
Do you think you got any better at managing your time and prioritising things?

18
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:09,400
You always used to say you had trouble with that...

19
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:14,620
Oh. definitely. There was so much pressure to meet the project deadline.

20
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:19,250
And I also got better at explaining things and asserting my opinions,

21
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:23,340
because I had to have weekly consultations with the marketing manager

22
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:25,810
and give him a progress report.

23
00:01:25,810 --> 00:01:28,570
It sounds as if you got a lot out of it then.

24
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:36,060
Absolutely. It was really worthwhile... But you know, the company benefited too...

25
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:38,280
Yes, they must have done.

26
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:45,516
After all, if they'd used a professional advertising agency to produce their brochure instead of doing it in-house,

27
00:01:45,516 --> 00:01:48,330
presumably they'd have paid a lot more?

28
00:01:48,330 --> 00:01:54,670
Oh, yes. I worked it out - it would have been 250 percent more.

29
00:01:54,670 --> 00:01:59,380
And I thought the end result was good, even though we did everything on site.

30
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:02,520
The company has quite a powerful computer

31
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:06,320
and I managed to borrow some scanning software from the university.

32
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:09,340
The new brochure looks really professional

33
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:12,570
it enhances the image of the company straight away.

34
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:17,020
So in the long run it should help them to attract clients

35
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:18,910
and improve their sales figures?

36
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:20,780
That's the idea. Yeah.

37
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:25,600
Well, all in all it sounds very positive

38
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,695
I think I will go ahead and apply for a placement myself.

39
00:02:28,695 --> 00:02:31,070
How do I go about it?

40
00:02:31,070 --> 00:02:33,895
It's easy enough to do,

41
00:02:33,895 --> 00:02:41,240
because there's a government agency called STEP - S-T-E-P - that organises placements for students.

42
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:43,512
You should start by getting their booklet

43
00:02:43,512 --> 00:02:47,730
with all the details - I expect you can download one from their website.

44
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:52,066
Actually, they've got copies in the psychology department - I've seen them there.

45
00:02:52,066 --> 00:02:55,680
I'll just go to the office and pick one up.

46
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:58,580
Right. And then if I were you

47
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:02,320
after I'd looked at it I'd go over all the options with someone...

48
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:08,150
I suppose I should ask my tutor's advice. He knows more about me than anyone.

49
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:10,801
One of the career officers would be better,

50
00:03:10,801 --> 00:03:15,440
they've got more knowledge about the jobs market than your personal tutor would have.

51
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:16,610
OK...

52
00:03:16,610 --> 00:03:20,920
And then when you know what you want you can register with STEP

53
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:22,710
you'll find their address in the booklet.

54
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:26,760
And once you've registered they assign you to a mentor

55
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:28,820
who looks after your application.

56
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:33,350
And then I suppose you just sit back and wait till you hear something?

57
00:03:33,350 --> 00:03:37,978
They told me at the careers office that it's best to be proactive,

58
00:03:37,978 --> 00:03:42,250
and get updates yourself by checking the website for new placement alerts.

59
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:47,080
Your mentor is supposed to keep you informed, but you can't rely on that.

60
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:52,910
I don't suppose it's a good idea to get in touch with companies directly, is it?

61
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:57,040
Not really. But it is the company who notifies you

62
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:58,820
if they want you to go for an interview.

63
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:03,550
You get a letter of invitation or an email from personnel departments.

64
00:04:03,550 --> 00:04:06,210
And do I reply directly to them?

65
00:04:06,210 --> 00:04:11,140
Yes, you do. STEP only gets involved again once you've been made a job offer.

66
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:15,000
Right... So once you've had an interview

67
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:18,070
you should let your mentor know what the outcome is?

68
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:23,200
I mean whether you're offered a job, and whether you've decided to accept it?

69
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:28,440
That's right. They'll inform the careers office once a placement has been agreed

70
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:30,360
so you don't have to do that.

71
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:32,440
Is that all then?

72
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:38,680
More or less. Only once you've accepted an offer you'll pRobably have to supply a reference,

73
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,800
because the placement will be conditional on that.

74
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:45,240
And that's something you should ask your own tutor to provide.

75
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:47,740
He knows about your academic ability

76
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,880
and also about your qualities, like reliability.

77
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:56,000
Well, thanks very much for the information - I'm starting to look forward...
